      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} Can this sender be faked by an attacker? \n\nI have experienced case yesterday that one user triggered teleport for all users in the instance by sending networked events to all players. We can't even tell the name of the attacker.\n\nI know that this could potentially be solved by adding an underscore before the name; but in some scenarios I want to compute users' interaction with local player on remote clients and communicate with local player through networked events. \n\nWill the attacker be able to fake the event （likely they will） and hide their names too if I implement sender check in the event handler? Is there server-side verification of the sender according to connection info?\n\nThank you. Looking forward to your reply!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
